{
  "abstract": "Lean 4 proof that for the random Littlewood polynomial f_n(z) = sum_{k <= n} eps_k z^k with independent uniform signs eps_k, it is not true that almost surely R_n / log n -> 2/pi, where R_n is the number of distinct real roots of f_n (the formal-conjectures statement Erdos521.erdos_521), and the same with R_n counted with multiplicity. For odd n = 2K - 1 the proof conditions on a cone event for the top coefficients (a two-dimensional walk staying in a quadrant, probability of order 1/K), bounds the real roots on that event by Descartes' rule of signs applied to f times a square of 1 + X + ... + X^N, estimates the sign-change probabilities of the resulting coefficient sums by Fourier inversion, and concludes with a second-moment (Kochen-Stone) argument that R_n < 0.63 log n + 2 infinitely often with positive probability.",
  "authors": [
